            <ArticleTitle>Protein-solvent interaction.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12551-017-0339-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Protein folding and assembly can be manipulated in in vitro systems by co-solvents at high concentrations. A number of co-solvents that enhance protein stability and assembly have been shown to be excluded from the protein surface. Such co-solvent exclusion has been demonstrated by dialysis experiments and shown to be correlated with their effects on protein stability and assembly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
